{"id": "EUVD-2026-103520", "enisaUuid": "6442d7c3-67bf-35df-be15-1fe17a7c1776", "description": "VideoLAN libdvdnav through 7.0.0 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in set_PTT that allows attackers to crash applications by supplying an invalid JumpTT title number checked only by an assert. Attackers can craft a DVD or disc image whose First Play program chain issues JumpTT with title 0 or an oversized number, reading past the heap title table and crashing the player.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T12:19:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:30:01", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libdvdnav-navigation-index-oob-read", "https://code.videolan.org/videolan/libdvdnav/-/blob/7.0.0/src/vm/getset.c#L51", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libdvdnav-through-7.0.0-out-of-bounds-read-via-set-ptt-jumptt"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hq5c-9qf4-9924", "CVE-2026-112058"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "aaca7715-c182-3884-9c10-d981b4bbdc09", "product": {"name": "libdvdnav", "vendor": {"name": "VideoLAN"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22647.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "00e6654e-004a-38f2-89c8-51e7fee9c723", "vendor": {"name": "VideoLAN"}}], "isExploited": false}